  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assignment Dutch Training and Exposure Programme (DUTEP) 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Dutch Training and Exposure Programme (DUTEP) is a public-private partnership to strategically enhance bilateral collaboration in terms of water management between Indonesia and the Netherlands. This assignment aims to support DUTEP 2026 in its impact and success, by fostering sustainable urban water management practices and strengthening the collaboration between Indonesia and the Netherlands. The assignment aims to strategically position DUTEP as part of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Water between the governments of the Netherlands and Indonesia, as a vehicle to foster knowledge exchange and participation of young professionals in the water domain. This strategic positioning entails the participation of DUTEP alumni and participants in various activities under the MoU Water. Additionally, it entails the active outreach to various sector organizations in the Netherlands as well as government authorities in Indonesia to participate in DUTEP and contribute to the scaling, reach and impact of DUTEP to secure its long-term continuation and anchoring.</narrative>
  </description>
